<title>SWEDEN: Scania sells 250 bus chassis to Eygpt, Ghana.</title>
<headline>Scania sells 250 bus chassis to Eygpt, Ghana.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish truck maker Scania AB said on Monday it had won an order for 250 bus chassis worth about 100 million crowns from Egyptian company Ghabbour Egypt and State Transport Company in Ghana.</p>
<p>Ghabbour Egypt will buy 200 chassis and State Transport Ghana will by 50, Scania said.</p>
<p>&quot;The order from Egypt follows an order for 144 bus chassis which Scania received in November last year,&quot; Rolf Teljeby, marketing head at Scania Buses &amp; Coaches, said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;For Scania the order to Ghana is a breakthrough at a new bus market.&quot;</p>
<p>The chassis to Egypt will be delivered between May and December, he said.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1006</p>
